      "chunkIndex": 2,
      "contentPreview": "THREE DELIBERATE POLICIES, NOT ONE RULE -- the finding that matters more than the count. Any plan proposing to unify ephemeral-alias handling across surfaces is proposing to break two of them.  (1) MCP facade: canonicalize and PROCEED. The server process persists, so an ephemeral memory is usable. (2) CLI: canonicalize then REFUSE (ScriniaCommands.cs:48-60). A CLI process exits immediately, so an ephemeral memory could never be read back. The refusal message deliberately names the CANONICAL form",
